{"tuid":"j49crlvd62mhwuzu","pageVersion":13,"fetchedAt":"2026-09-30T09:55:56.751Z","record":{"colophon":{"generator":"ifdb.org/viewgame","generatorversion":1,"originated":"2025-03-25"},"identification":{"ifids":["ZCODE-1-990528-9252"],"bafn":431,"format":"zcode"},"bibliographic":{"title":"Aisle","author":"Sam Barlow","language":"en","firstpublished":"1999-05-28","genre":"Slice of life","description":"&quot;Late Thursday night. You&#039;ve had a hard day and the last thing you need is this: shopping. Luckily, the place is pretty empty and you&#039;re progressing rapidly. On to the next aisle... <br> <br><i>Aisle started out as a game which would not need the usual meta-verbs... i.e. a game with only one turn. The initial idea was: How do I make a game with only one turn interesting? Give it lots of endings--in fact there are many &#039;endings&#039; and (hopefully) every sensible action results in an &#039;ending&#039;. There is no winning action. There is however more going on than just this and the more endings you see the more things should become clear.</i>&quot; [--blurb from The Z-Files Catalogue]"},"contacts":[],"ifdb":{"tuid":"j49crlvd62mhwuzu","pageversion":13,"link":"https://ifdb.org/viewgame?id=j49crlvd62mhwuzu","coverart":{"url":"https://ifdb.org/coverart?id=j49crlvd62mhwuzu&version=13"},"playTimeInMinutes":7,"primaryPlayOnlineUrl":"https://iplayif.com/?story=https%3A%2F%2Fifarchive.org%2Fif-archive%2Fgames%2Fzcode%2FAisle.z5","downloads":{"links":[{"url":"http://www.ifarchive.org/if-archive/games/zcode/Aisle.z5","playOnlineUrl":"https://iplayif.com/?story=https%3A%2F%2Fifarchive.org%2Fif-archive%2Fgames%2Fzcode%2FAisle.z5","title":"Aisle.z5","isGame":true,"format":"zcode"},{"url":"http://www.ifarchive.org/if-archive/solutions/Aisle.wlk","title":"Aisle.wlk","desc":"Walkthrough","format":"text"},{"url":"http://allthingsjacq.com/intfic_clubfloyd_20170601.html","title":"ClubFloyd transcript","format":"html"},{"url":"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Vid